From 71efd59a0957bd0c0c71932ab7381bae2a0892ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaloyan Naumov <knaumov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:36:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0014a-b70-offload-trace: env-gated KV-offload instrumentation
 (B70_OFFLOAD_TRACE=1)

Default off; with the flag unset the connector behaves as upstream.
With B70_OFFLOAD_TRACE=1 the offloading scheduler logs, prefix B70-OFFLOAD:
- lookup: per request, per group kind (full/mamba/swa) the hit-chunk range and
  HIT/HIT_PENDING/RETRY/MISS counts, the group that zeroed the request, and
  request.shared_prefix_boundary;
- handoff: aligned Mamba/GDN boundary hand-offs offered vs stored per request;
- store/load/partial-tail-store: job ids, reachable_boundaries, keys per kind;
- req-done: store/load jobs submitted vs completed when a request is dropped;
- state (daemon thread, every B70_OFFLOAD_TRACE_PERIOD_S, default 60 s, so it
  also fires at idle): write-pending chunks and bytes, ready chunks, evictable,
  per-kind resident/pending key counts, in-flight jobs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
